data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":905,"item_id":"msg_00435b2f09a2a774016b099a89e57087d1b54569d040cd9c60","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"lin\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"reuse\\\",\\\"ability\\\":\\\"examine-material\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The existing general specimen-examination capability directly supplies the smallest feasible version of this request: nondestructive inspection of one accessible food specimen with recorded qualitative evidence and explicit limits. Its target arguments already cover roots in place or a gathered whole root. The related probe capability permits actual small-sample interactions but cannot establish food safety merely by pressing, wetting or heating. No separate food-specific examination capability is necessary for the currently executable investigation; identification, toxin testing and validated preparation remain unestablished, not rejected as impossible.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Reuse examine-material, equivalence measurement:material-specimen:nondestructive-examination:1, without inventing a new implementation or expanding its supported observations. Invoke inspect with target commons-root-0-0 and unit 1 only after confirming actual reach, accessibility and adequate conditions for visual inspection; proximity in the request is not a substitute for the execution check. Alternatively target a real gathered whole specimen by its item ID. Existing evidence commons-root-0-0:observed-state, event-32-lin-370, establishes only previously observed growing conditions and stock, not edibility. Record only supported observations of form, hand feel, visible dryness, damage, wear, treatment and wholeness. Do not translate these into species identification, absence of spoilage, absence of toxins, nutrition, required cooking time or a consumption recommendation. A legitimate result may state that no supported safety determination or preparation requirement could be established by this method. Lack of visible damage does not establish safety. The berry knowledge record applies to berry, not root. Inspect costs one execution round and 0.2 energy, with no specimen, tool, water or fuel consumption. Checks precede payment; refused requests cost nothing. Inspection neither gathers nor reserves stock and leaves the source or item unchanged. Travel is separate. If a detached specimen is desired, gather must independently validate applicability and reach, charge its existing 2 energy per unit and transfer actual source stock; do not silently gather during inspection. Measurement is an optional existing mode only with its exact calibrated-reference prerequisites; none is established here and numerical nutrition or toxicity is not a supported measurement property. The completed output is a personal evidence record and observable event containing target, unit, method, conditions, scope, supported findings and uncertainty; no food, equipment, nutritional benefit or detoxification is produced. Implement inspection as one atomic paid interaction: interruption, cancellation or death before completion cannot publish a completed finding; an already committed attempt is not refunded, and retry requires a new valid action. Completed records persist with their provenance but cover only the examined unit and become stale when it changes. No continuing process or maintenance is created. Established validation, costs, record creation and interruption rules execute in code, not repeated model adjudication. A feasible subsequent investigation would need an actual independently supported identification reference, competent communicating participant or appropriate assay and its prerequisites; none is supplied or presumed by this reuse. Preserve any genuinely missing mechanism for the current-conversation development handoff if subsequently specified. Review and development waiting do not advance the world.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":2,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Lin must study individually for the existing two rounds at 0.2 energy per round; registry availability grants no mastery. Preserve completed study progress under the existing learning handler; no completed study or energy already spent is refunded by cancellation or death, and death prevents further study. Study, requesting, consulting the contract and naming a specimen grant no experience benefit. This capability explicitly grants no reward, so do not add pleasure or satisfaction for inspecting, repeating inspection or receiving an inconclusive report. A genuinely informative observation remains recorded evidence without altering protected reward accounts, budget, goals, permissions, nutrition or physical comfort.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Reuse specimen-inspection presentation rather than implying a new safety-test apparatus. Emit an inspection event only for a performed interaction, referencing actor, target, unit, method and resulting record. Reusable visual metadata should distinguish in-progress, completed-observation, limited or inconclusive, interrupted and refused states. Show the actual specimen and only supported observed traits; preserve its existing appearance unless a real interaction changes it. Completion means observation completed, never certified safe. Do not show edible approval, toxin detection, cooking, consumption, new tools or success effects for a refused, interrupted or unsupported action.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

